`Session` / `Host` with native Python values over `ctypes`
([`pancake`](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/bindings/python/pancake)).
Transports: `pancake.tcp`, `pancake.inproc`, lazy `pancake.iroh`. Install:
[Bindings]($link.page('bindings')).

## The same round-trip

The [Start building]($link.page('start')) round-trip (connect, fetch, send,
handle the reply) reads like this in Python. Start `serve` yourself (Rust
auto-serves on `connect`); `fetch` / `send` also start the inbound loop on
demand.

> []($block.attrs('code-tabs'))
> **tcp**
> ```python
> from pancake import connect, tcp_locator
>
> # tcp: the peer is a place, a cleartext host and port.
> partner = tcp_locator("127.0.0.1", 9099)
>
> session = await connect(partner)
> session.serve()
>
> greeter = await session.fetch("greeter")  # a capability, by name
> try:
>     reply = await session.send(greeter, "greet", ["world"])
>     print(reply)
> except Exception as reason:
>     print(f"the greeter refused: {reason}")
>
> await session.close()
> ```
> **iroh**
> ```python
> from pancake import connect
> from pancake.iroh import Reachability
>
> # iroh reachability: the peer is a key, not a place. DISCOVERY resolves
> # the bare node id over the open internet; no address in hand.
> partner = "ocapn://3b6a…da29.iroh"
>
> session = await connect(partner, Reachability.DISCOVERY)
> session.serve()
>
> greeter = await session.fetch("greeter")  # a capability, by name
> try:
>     reply = await session.send(greeter, "greet", ["world"])
>     print(reply)
> except Exception as reason:
>     print(f"the greeter refused: {reason}")
>
> await session.close()
> ```

The iroh tab is a bare node id plus posture; fetch/send match the tcp tab.
Dial-by-id and discovery: [iroh]($link.page('transports/iroh')).

## Async

[`asyncio`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/asyncio.html). Hold a `Session`;
`await session.send(...)` for a result; `session.serve()` runs the inbound loop
until close (start it yourself, unlike Rust). CapTP ideas:
[Concepts]($link.page('concepts')).

## Actors

`behavior(verb, args)` on `session.spawn` / `session.publish`. One trampoline
into Python per deliver.

## Binding check and example

```sh
zig build python-dogfood    # the Python consumer against the pancake archives
```

The full surface lives in the
[Python binding README](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/bindings/python/README.md),
and the
[rooms chat client](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/examples/apps/rooms/python/room_client.py)
builds a small capability-secure room on this surface.
